From 5089e62fb2719631edc179f840886be549b34d6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iimmyy <i.a.martins001@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:59:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hexagon: full data-cache clean+invalidate before every
 FLASH_ATTN_EXT, so fresh runs of the same input give the same numbers.
 Before, the same prompt at temperature 0 gave different word scores within
 1-5 words from one process to the next (and NPU-drafted replies never matched
 undrafted ones). Per-op fingerprints were identical with <= 8 ops per batch
 and differed at a moving spot with 16+; a save-only flush does not cure it,
 so an op reads a stale cached copy of memory written behind the cache.
 Clearing before ROPE or RMS_NORM also cures it, before SET_ROWS or once per
 batch does not; the stale reader is not named yet. Cost ~4% (decode 7.60 ->
 7.27 tok/s). examples/lg-fingerprint: per-op output hashes (LG_FP_MATCH) and
 per-word score hashes

---
 examples/CMakeLists.txt                    |  1 +
 examples/lg-fingerprint/CMakeLists.txt     |  5 ++
 examples/lg-fingerprint/lg-fingerprint.cpp | 95 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/main.c           | 10 +++
 4 files changed, 111 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 examples/lg-fingerprint/CMakeLists.txt
 create mode 100644 examples/lg-fingerprint/lg-fingerprint.cpp

diff --git a/examples/CMakeLists.txt b/examples/CMakeLists.txt
index 39f802d..93b9ef1 100644
--- a/examples/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/examples/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ else()
     add_subdirectory(debug)
     add_subdirectory(embedding)
     add_subdirectory(eval-callback)
